From: EglantinePS5 <noreply@eglantineps5.local>
Subject: [PATCH] EDEN_UP_TC_KEEP_REMADE=1: the collectors keep large converted ASTC, and converted ASTC the game makes again after a collector deleted it, as EDEN_NX2_TC_KEEP_ASYNC keeps AsynchronousDecode images (Lichii #1129's alternative); EDEN_UP_TC_TRACE=1 logs each image made and deleted (Lichii #1130); off by default

Lossless: no texture changes format, size or levels. Only when an image is deleted changes.

Credits. EDEN_UP_TC_KEEP_REMADE is the alternative liomaroliveira names at the end of
zortos293/Lichii #1129 (open, head 49a1cd23f9, "scale the collector's ceiling with the device
budget on 10+ GiB cards"): exempt CostlyLoad images the collector evicted and the game re-created
within N frames. #1129's own change (raise the critical ceiling from a 10 GiB budget on) does
nothing on the PS5, whose budget is 6 GiB; its alternative is written here from the PR text, not
from code. EDEN_UP_TC_TRACE is a port of zortos293/Lichii #1130 (open, head 92b29fb513, by
liomaroliveira, upstream name EDEN_NX2_TC_TRACE). Neither is compiled or run upstream by us.

Why. EDEN_NX2_TC_KEEP_ASYNC (0232, live switch since 0478) only covers AsynchronousDecode images,
and vk_texture_cache.cpp sets that flag only when the RGBA8 decode is over
EDEN_NX2_GPU_TRANSCODE_MIB. The play env sets 256, so Ocarina of Time's 6144x6144 ASTC ground
texture (13 levels, 192 MiB decode, 48 MiB as BC3, flags 0x1073: AcceleratedUpload, Converted,
CostlyLoad) goes to the GPU transcode and is protected only as CostlyLoad. That ends in aggressive
mode, which PoolPressure level 2 turns on. Each new copy then needs the 192 MiB decode image and
a 48 MiB BC3 output again. t85-f run704: four refusals of that decode image in 20 s. Runs
739/742/743: made 3 times each. batch-t89-b run759 (pool hog 1024): decode images for the 6144 at
83.2 s and again at 91.0 s, the second together with two 3072x3072 ones (48 MiB decode each), then
"Out of device memory: keeping 1536 MiB more free". run761 (hog 1280) made the 6144 once at 81.4 s
and ran out of device memory at 90.5 s, about where run759 made it again. #1129 saw the same set on a 12 GB card: the 6144 and three 3072x3072
ASTC 5x5 textures deleted by the aggressive collector and made again ~128 frames later.

EDEN_UP_TC_KEEP_REMADE=1 (Common::PeSwitch, exact 1).
- Candidates: ASTC the host does not sample as ASTC (Converted), CostlyLoad, not
  AsynchronousDecode (those stay KEEP_ASYNC's, whatever it is set to, so this switch changes
  nothing for the CPU-decoded 1365x1365x90 arrays), backed whole (not Unbacked, UnwrittenSparse,
  SparseLayers or SparseTiles), holding at most 256 MiB of device memory (the >1 GiB RGBA8 huge
  arrays are never kept).
- Kept from creation when the RGBA8 decode (every level and layer, the sum
  TranscodeScratchTooLarge uses) is over EDEN_UP_TC_KEEP_REMADE_MIB (digits 0..4096, default
  128 = the default GPU transcode limit, so with GPU_TRANSCODE_MIB=256 it covers exactly the images
  KEEP_ASYNC lost; 0: none this way). In Ocarina: the 6144x6144.
- Kept when made again: a collector (any reason starting with "gc", below) deleted a candidate at
  the same GPU address with the same format, width, height, levels and layers at most 600 frames
  before, and its decode is at least EDEN_UP_TC_KEEP_REMADE_MIN_MIB (digits 0..4096, default 32;
  0: none this way). In Ocarina: the 3072x3072 ASTC (48 MiB decode, 12 MiB as BC3), from their
  second creation on. Up to 64 deletes are remembered; older than 600 frames go first.
- A kept image is skipped at every place KEEP_ASYNC's images are skipped: RunGarbageCollector
  (except its old pass: unused for EDEN_NX2_TC_OLD_AGE frames, 1800 unset, under high priority, as
  KEEP_ASYNC), CollectForBuffer, AreaEvict, RefusalEvict and RefusalDownloadEvict. Unmaps and
  joins delete it as before (the Fritchii cold sweep never takes Converted images). Guest writes
  still mark it CpuModified and upload it again (new decode image and all), as before: keeping is
  only about the collectors.
- New ImageBase fields tc_keep_remade / tc_keep_remade_frame, set only here, only with the
  switch on. No new ImageFlagBits bit (0495 adds GuestBytes = 1 << 24 at the same place).
- HW_GPU lines, the first 64 of each kind and then each power of two:
  "EDEN_UP_TC_KEEP_REMADE: keeping <addr> WxHxL (n levels, format F): decode D MiB, over N
  MiB; holds H MiB; K kept now, T so far" or "...: made again F frames after a collector deleted
  it, decode D MiB; ...", and "EDEN_UP_TC_KEEP_REMADE: kept <addr> WxHxL deleted (reason) F
  frames after it was kept; K kept now, D deleted so far".

EDEN_UP_TC_TRACE=1 (Common::PeSwitch, exact 1). As #1130: LOG_WARNING HW_GPU "TCTRACE create
id= gpu= type= fmt= WxHxD lv= ly= guest=KiB joined= found= ms= frame=" after JoinImages (format
as upstream) and "TCTRACE delete id= gpu= fmt= WxHxD guest=KiB immediate= reason= frame=" in
DeleteImage. Reasons: gc, gc-high-priority, gc-aggressive (as upstream), and ours: gc-old (the old
pass), gc-buffer (CollectForBuffer), gc-area (AreaEvict), gc-refusal (RefusalEvict),
gc-refusal-copied (RefusalDownloadEvict), cold (EDEN_UP_FRITCHII_COLD), unmap, join, join-ignored
(as upstream), other. Also ours: "TCTRACE refused gpu= type= fmt= WxHxD lv= ly= guest=KiB frame="
when JoinImages makes nothing, so a refused first creation is told apart from a delete and a new
make. EDEN_UP_TC_TRACE_MIB=<N> (digits 0..4096; unset or 0: every image, as upstream): only
images of at least N MiB of guest memory. Ocarina makes ~6500 images per 600 frames in the
village, so use =4 on the console (the 6144 is 31 MiB of guest data, a 3072x3072 about 8 MiB).
The reason pointer is set before each DeleteImage call even with both switches off (a pointer
store, nothing read); DeleteImage reads it and puts back "other".

Interplay.
- EDEN_NX2_TC_KEEP_ASYNC: separate rule for separate images, same exemption sites. With
  GPU_TRANSCODE_MIB at its default (128) the large rule finds nothing (every ASTC over 128 MiB is
  AsynchronousDecode) and only the made-again rule acts.
- EDEN_NX2_GPU_TRANSCODE_MIB / TRANSCODE_KEEP_MIB / TRANSCODE_WAIT: routing is untouched. A kept
  6144 needs its 192 MiB decode image once per area visit instead of once per collector delete.
  EDEN_UP_ASTC_BATCH_MIB (separate draft) shrinks each decode; this one cuts how many there are.
  No file in common.
- Ahead guard (0491-0504, 0511): no texture cache code there; texture data is "not covered" by
  the guard and guest writes still upload kept images (0502).
- Skip-stale uploads (0495): a kept image is not deleted, so the collector does not MarkStale it;
  ASTC images carry GuestBytes with 0495 on, which MarkStale refuses anyway. When a kept image
  does go (old pass), the old path runs.
- AREA_EVICT (play env =40): kept images are skipped as KEEP_ASYNC's are. This keeps the 6144
  through a door (house and back), which is where its remake hit. It goes after 1800 unused
  frames under pressure (old pass).
- Port script (prepare-vulkan-port.py): no anchor changes. The pinned RunGarbageCollector anchors
  ("(!high_priority_mode && must_download)) {", the Configure lines, the drain block,
  "if (must_download) {", the Cleanup capture), "namespace VideoCommon {" and the DeleteImage
  accounting segment (HasScaled to gpu_addr) each still occur once and are unchanged; the new
  DeleteImage block sits before that segment.

Expected memory effect (not measured). Per remake of the 6144 that this avoids: a 192 MiB decode
image + 48 MiB BC3 output (+ the 31 MiB guest upload), ~240 MiB at the moment it happened, 3 to 4
times per walk in t85-f and run739-743. Per 3072x3072 remake: ~60 MiB (48 + 12). In run759 at
91.0 s the 6144 and two 3072s came together: ~360 MiB. Cost: the kept images stay while unused,
48 MiB for the 6144, 12 MiB per 3072 (84 MiB with EDEN_UP_TC_KEEP_REMADE_MIB=32, which keeps the
3072s from their first creation too). It does not help a first creation the pool refuses
(run759's 32 EDEN_REFUSED_IMAGE lines for the 48 MiB BC3 image itself).

Unset (or anything but exactly "1"): KeepRemadeCandidate is false, no ImageBase field is ever
set, KeptRemade is false at every site, nothing is remembered or logged; collectors, InsertImage
and DeleteImage behave as before. EDEN_UP_TC_TRACE unset: no line. The size variables are only
read with their switch on.

Not built, not run. git apply --check passes on T88 core and on T88 with the series 0491-0515
(texture cache files; 0495 and 0498 touch them), also on top of draft-memory-census.patch.
Checked by reading only.
